   "summary": "The guide describes Japan’s national, regional, and local economic controls, including ministries, Control Societies and Associations, Munitions Companies, National Policy Companies, and Eidan. It recommends retaining useful administrative records and regional structures while abolishing wartime control bodies, screening senior personnel, and encouraging smaller civilian producers. Proposed occupation controls include production priorities, material allocations, credit, regular reports, and central and regional production agencies. The document continues beyond page 112.",
